\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Blessed life! the heart at rest
\par When all without tumultous seems-
\par That trusts a higher will, and deems 
\par that higher will, not mine, the best.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O blessed life! the mind that sees,
\par Whatever change the years may bring,
\par A mercy still in everything,
\par And shining through all mysteries.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O blessed life! the soul that soars,
\par When sense of mortal sight is dim,
\par Beyond the sense-beyond to Him
\par Whose love unlocks the heavenly doors
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O blessed life! heart, mind, and soul,
\par From self-born aims and wishes free,
\par In all at one with Diety,
\par And loyal to  the Lord's control.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O life, how blessed, how divine!
\par High life, the earnest of higher:
\par Saviour, fulfil my deep desire,
\par And let this blessed life be mine.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

